# Copy to .env only if you need to override a default. The dashboard works
# with no .env at all in both normal setups:
#   - start-prod.bat: FastAPI serves this build itself — same origin, any port.
#   - start.bat (dev): Vite proxies /api to localhost:8000 (see vite.config.ts).
#
# Vite only exposes variables prefixed with VITE_ to the browser, and it reads
# them at BUILD/DEV-SERVER START — restart `npm run dev` after changing this.

# Only needed if the frontend is served from somewhere OTHER than the backend
# AND that backend isn't on localhost:8000 (the dev proxy's default target) —
# e.g. running the Vite dev server against a backend on a different port.
# VITE_API_BASE_URL=http://localhost:8000

# Recordings sent to Gemini per click of "Run Analysis".
# Leave this commented out to use the backend's own PIPELINE_RUN_LIMIT
# (backend/.env), which is the recommended place to set it — one setting,
# enforced server-side. Uncomment only to override from the browser side.
# Set to 0 to lift the cap and process the whole backlog in one click.
# VITE_PIPELINE_LIMIT=5
